  "body": "From the independent re-review of PR #346 (#330), also true for the single-face pick and the 3-2-1 work-offset alignment (#187).\n\nFace outward normals for alignment picks come from the facets' winding (`outward_normal`, used by `crates/app/src/pick/plane.rs` and `pick/align.rs`). Nothing checks the winding against the solid itself, so a model whose triangles are wound inside-out (a common STL export fault) gives inverted normals: \"lay this face on G17\" then turns the part upside down, and a 3-2-1 picks the opposite side, with no warning. Mis-orientation is gouge-class.\n\n**Done means:** at import (or on first use), each closed body's winding is checked against its signed volume; an inside-out body is either repaired (all facets flipped, with a load note naming the body) or refused by name for alignment picks (\"Face 12 belongs to a body whose facets are inside-out ...\"); an open/non-manifold body whose outside can't be determined refuses face-normal picks by name. Pinned by tests with an inverted-winding cube for the plane pick, the two-edge pick and the 3-2-1.\n\nRelated: #330 (PR #346), #187, #326.\n",
